<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/059Q">Corollary <span data-tag="059Q">4.7.9.17</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category, let $n$ be an integer, and let $A \subseteq B$ be simplicial sets. If $B$ has dimension $\leq n+1$, then every lifting problem </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@C =50pt@R=50pt{ A \ar [d] \ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\ar [d] \\ B \ar [r] \ar@ {--&gt;}[ur] &amp;  \operatorname {h}_{\mathit{\leq {}n}}{\mathit{(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})}} } \]
</div>
<p> has a solution. If $B$ has dimension $\leq n-1$, then the solution is unique. </p>
